# House Price Visualization, Spatial Analytics & Real-Estate Insights

## Project Overview

This project analyzes the King County House Sales Dataset using Python. It focuses on visualizing house prices, exploring geographical patterns, and identifying important factors that influence real-estate prices.

## Objectives

- Understand and analyze house sales data.
- Visualize house price distributions.
- Explore the relationship between living area and house prices.
- Analyze house prices based on the number of bedrooms.
- Perform spatial analysis using latitude and longitude.
- Identify correlations between property features and sale prices.
- Generate useful real-estate insights.

## Dataset

**Dataset Name:** King County House Sales Dataset

**File Name:** `kc_house_data.csv`

The dataset contains house sale records from King County, Washington, USA.

Important columns include:
- `price` — Sale price of the house
- `bedrooms` — Number of bedrooms
- `bathrooms` — Number of bathrooms
- `sqft_living` — Interior living area in square feet
- `sqft_lot` — Lot area in square feet
- `yr_built` — Year the house was built
- `zipcode` — Property ZIP code
- `lat` — Latitude
- `long` — Longitude

